      "instructions": "Settings menu design (render/settings.ts + render/audio.ts). A centered panel (getTexture('panel.settings'), 320x400) over a dark overlay, with a gear icon (getTexture('icon.gear')) beside a \"SETTINGS\" title, and a BACK button (getTexture('button.back')) at the bottom that plays audioManager.playSound('sfx.back') and returns to the previous screen.\n\nRows, top to bottom:\n1. MUSIC toggle — ON/OFF, getTexture('toggle.on')/('toggle.off'); plays sfx.toggle on change; audioManager.setMusicEnabled(bool).\n2. SFX toggle — ON/OFF, same toggle sprites; plays sfx.toggle on change.\n3. VIBRATION toggle — ON/OFF, same toggle sprites; plays sfx.toggle on change.\n4. MUSIC VOLUME slider — a draggable volume slider (SEPARATE from SFX).\n5. SFX VOLUME slider — a draggable volume slider (SEPARATE from music).\n\nVOLUME SLIDERS (the focus of this spec) — there are TWO independent sliders, one for music and one for sfx (NOT a single master volume):\n- Each slider row = a label (\"MUSIC VOL\" / \"SFX VOL\"), a track Sprite getTexture('slider.track') (200x16), and a draggable knob Sprite getTexture('slider.knob') (20x28) positioned on the track.\n- The knob is draggable (pointerdown on the knob -> pointermove drags -> pointerup releases; clamp the knob x to the track ends). The knob's x position along the track maps to a volume value in [0,1] (left edge = 0, right edge = 1).\n- On drag, update the value live and persist it: localStorage 'rs_setting_music_vol' for the music slider and 'rs_setting_sfx_vol' for the sfx slider (store the float 0..1). Load these on show()/init and place each knob to reflect the saved value (default music 0.5, sfx 0.6).\n- Music slider changes call audioManager.setMusicVolume(v); SFX slider changes call audioManager.setSfxVolume(v). Optionally play sfx.toggle (a soft tick) on sfx-slider release so the user hears the level.\n\nAUDIO WIRING (render/audio.ts) — the AudioManager ALREADY has separate _musicGain and _sfxGain GainNodes:\n- Add setMusicVolume(v: number): clamp v to [0,1] and set this._musicGain.gain.value = v (guard null ctx).\n- Add setSfxVolume(v: number): clamp v to [0,1] and set this._sfxGain.gain.value = v (guard null ctx).\n- When the AudioContext is first created (_getCtx), initialise _musicGain/_sfxGain from the persisted 'rs_setting_music_vol'/'rs_setting_sfx_vol' (falling back to the current defaults 0.5 / 0.6) so a saved volume applies on boot.\n\nKeep the existing Music/SFX/Vibration toggles and BACK button working. This is a UI/feel/layout change verified visually (no sim test). Do NOT edit game/test/** or game/accept/**.",
